WEBVTT


00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.300
www. opensubtitles. org
- Omerta -


00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.600
Well, I'm just a smalltown cop,
Mostly I give out parking tickets.


00:00:25.635 --> 00:00:27.600
<i>I don't wanna talk about your work.</i>


00:00:27.635 --> 00:00:30.900
Ok... How are things in L.A.?


00:00:30.935 --> 00:00:31.865
<i>Jesse...</i>


00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.700
- Why'd you call me
at the office, Jenn?


00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.200
<i>I don't want you to call me tonight.</i>


00:00:39.235 --> 00:00:40.665
Ok.


00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.600
<i>Actually, I don't think
we should talk for a while.</i>


00:00:43.635 --> 00:00:45.567
How long, a while?


00:00:45.602 --> 00:00:47.500
<i>I don't know.</i>


00:00:47.535 --> 00:00:49.665
Ok.


00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.700
<i>So, now it's coming over.</i>


00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.400
<i>He thinks it's strange
that we still talk every night.</i>


00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.900
Was he there last night?


00:00:59.935 --> 00:01:01.917
<i>Yes.</i>


00:01:01.952 --> 00:01:03.900
Ok.


00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.500
<i>Do you understand?</i>


00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:09.465
No.


00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.200
<i>Are you alright?</i>


00:01:11.235 --> 00:01:12.165
Yeah...


00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:18.200
<i>Jesse... Thank you.</i>


00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.400
Things get this slow
when Lou was Chief?


00:01:38.435 --> 00:01:41.100
All the time. How's your wife?


00:01:41.135 --> 00:01:42.800
Ex-wife, Rose.


00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.600
- The Rabid skunk has benn dispatched.
- How?


00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.665
D'Angelo shot him.


00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:51.965
- Ok.
- D'Angelo was not happy...


00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.565
- What did he say?
- He said "Why it is always my fault?"


00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.300
Hey, I didn't say it was his fault,
I just said I was blaming him for it.


00:01:58.335 --> 00:01:59.765
He thinks you pick on him.


00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:01.002
Well, I don't like him.


00:02:01.003 --> 00:02:03.232
If you don't like him,
why don't you fire him?


00:02:03.435 --> 00:02:07.465
I'm not gonna fire him,
I'm gonna wear him down.


00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.665
Wednesday is your town council meeting.
Oh, I'm gonna be late tommorrow...


00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.094
I have to take Brian to the orthodontist.


00:02:12.095 --> 00:02:14.895
And Edwin says the Civil War
Memorial was falling down.


00:02:14.935 --> 00:02:16.427
He's watering too much.


00:02:16.428 --> 00:02:18.328
Well, he wants the square to
look good for the Fall Regatta.


00:02:18.335 --> 00:02:19.665
- Did you tell him?
- Yes.


00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.100
- What did he say?
- He wants to know, how you know?


00:02:22.135 --> 00:02:25.400
I'm the police chief, I know everything.


00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.550
They said it might be vandalism.


00:02:27.585 --> 00:02:29.400
Tell them he's watering to much.


00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:58.865
- Brahms.
- Excuse me?


00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.150
I'm Hilda Evans, Chief Stone.


00:03:02.185 --> 00:03:05.365
How's the drinking thing going?


00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.700
Small town. Ever since people heard
that you were drunk on your job interview...


00:03:09.735 --> 00:03:11.465
...there's been concern.


00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.500
Actually I drank too much the night before.
I just made the mistake...


00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:17.265
...of having one in the
morning to steady up.


00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:22.400
Brahms. When I'm feeling troubled,
I sit in my favourite chair...


00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:26.100
...put my head back, and listen to Brahms.


00:03:26.135 --> 00:03:30.600
I find it comforting. Enough said.


00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.900
Wake up!


00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.565
I know you can hear me.


00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.200
Doctor says your wound's
completely healed.


00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:04.565
Believe it or not,
Melbourne, Australia.


00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:07.600
A man left comatose for over
ten years, suddenly sat bolt...


00:04:07.635 --> 00:04:10.900
...upright and said
"I'll have a cappuccino."


00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:21.300
Well, everything happens
at once, Suitcase.


00:04:21.335 --> 00:04:23.400
Things are really jumping in Paradise.


00:04:23.435 --> 00:04:25.400
Rampant crime.


00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.618
I just heard at
the weekly briefing...


00:04:27.619 --> 00:04:31.027
... that there's a drug ring
trying to set up in our town.


00:04:31.062 --> 00:04:34.500
I could use a little backup!


00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:41.300
Suit, we're four people police force.
With Molly out, I got to retrain Rose...


00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:48.800
The town council wants me to replace you.


00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.765
"It was bitter cold"


00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:08.300
"The wind in his face made it difficult
to grasp the shape before him. "


00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:12.400
"The bow of the yacht cut through
the sea, needly cleaving the water... "


00:05:12.435 --> 00:05:14.565
"... into mirror image waves. "


00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:17.818
"Now he saw the ship
with in its full glory..."


00:05:17.819 --> 00:05:23.019
"...80 feet at least,
mahogany hull in full sail, dark and silent. "


00:05:23.135 --> 00:05:26.000
"A latter day Flying Dutchman. "


00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.600
ROBERT B. PARKER'S
JESSE STONE


00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.100
SEA CHANGE


00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:18.100
Nice car.


00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:21.000
Are you giving me a ticket?


00:08:21.035 --> 00:08:22.867
- It depends.
- On what?


00:08:22.902 --> 00:08:24.665
If this is your car...


00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:26.800
You don't hink I can own a car like this?


00:08:26.835 --> 00:08:28.900
- I didn't say that.
- It's not mine.


00:08:28.935 --> 00:08:31.965
Then I'm not giving you a ticket.


00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.700
Look, the owner's
just been in a week...


00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:37.600
- ...He came up for Race Week.
- Race Week.


00:08:37.635 --> 00:08:40.217
Race Week is good for local business, right?


00:08:40.252 --> 00:08:42.800
- It is.
- Ok, why give him the ticket?


00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.265
The curb is red.


00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:47.065
What if it were my car?


00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:50.900
I'm still give it a ticket,
but with infinitely more regret.


00:08:50.935 --> 00:08:54.265
- So, are you feeling regret?
- A little.


00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.900
Alright, it's not hard to fix that.
Tear it up!


00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.165
No.


00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:02.600
You gonna get me
in trouble, don't you.


00:09:02.635 --> 00:09:03.565
No.


00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.300
And you are feeling regret.


00:09:06.335 --> 00:09:08.700
Yes.


00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.465
Don't you have anything better to do...


00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:20.100
...then spend your time
with writing parking tickets?


00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.100
No.


00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:53.265
<i>Hi jesse, it's Jenn.</i>


00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:57.600
<i>I guess you are left,
I'll call you at the office.</i>


00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:25.900
- Hello?
- It's me.


00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:28.265
What's wrong?


00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:32.300
Nothing, I just wanted to see
how you're doing, Molly.


00:12:32.335 --> 00:12:35.017
Fine... You?


00:12:35.052 --> 00:12:37.665
I woke you up.


00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:39.065
<i>Oh no, you didn't, I'm...</i>


00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:41.800
...too uncomfortable to sleep.


00:12:41.835 --> 00:12:45.500
What time is it?


00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:52.200
9 o'clock in L.A.
How is Jenn?


00:12:52.235 --> 00:12:54.100
Fine.


00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:55.750
You Ok?


00:12:55.785 --> 00:12:57.165
<i>Yes.</i>


00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:59.300
Would you tell me, if you're worrying?


00:12:59.335 --> 00:13:00.665
No.


00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:03.500
<i>There's a lot of people
care about you, Jesse.</i>


00:13:03.535 --> 00:13:05.100
Including you?


00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:07.400
Especially me.


00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:10.200
So you think you gonna
have the kid early?


00:13:10.235 --> 00:13:13.300
Hopefully not too early.


00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:15.365
How's Rose doing?


00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:17.100
She's a little rusty,
but she's doing fine.


00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:19.700
Did you see Suitcase today?


00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:20.800
<i>Every day.</i>


00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:22.700
Did you give him my love?


00:13:22.735 --> 00:13:25.200
I forgot.


00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:27.865
Oh, did you have the test?


00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:33.200
Oh, the baby's fine.
I'm what's termed the "high risk" mother.


00:13:33.235 --> 00:13:35.600
Means "old".


00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:41.300
Jesse, I need to get some sleep.


00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:47.700
- I woke you up.
- Will you call me tomorrow?


00:13:47.735 --> 00:13:50.400
Ugh, sure.


00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:06.100
- So, nobody called?
- I don't do phones.


00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:11.650
- You go now?
- Aham, in a while.


00:16:11.685 --> 00:16:14.300
'Cause we're almost
out of coffee.


00:16:14.335 --> 00:16:16.700
I think you should get some.


00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:22.000
Alright, I'll buy it.


00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.700
- Ugh, Skipper, I...
- Not today, D'Angelo.


00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:44.400
- Are you alright?
- I'm fine.


00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:55.800
You can't come every couple of months,
and expect to get anything done.


00:16:55.835 --> 00:16:59.565
I've been busy.
Fighting crime.


00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:04.200
- It's small town, What do you wait?
- What I've come to expect.


00:17:04.235 --> 00:17:07.365
You take a job you're overqualified for.


00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:11.300
You're good at what you do, so you
stir the pot up comes a couple of rats


00:17:11.335 --> 00:17:15.400
but for all intents and purposes,
nothing happens here.


00:17:15.435 --> 00:17:19.117
You know what I'm
talking about, you're a cop.


00:17:19.152 --> 00:17:22.800
- Yeah, but I quit.
- Because it made you drink?


00:17:22.835 --> 00:17:26.100
I think that's called "projection".


00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:31.250
- So... You called me.
- In a moment of weakness.


00:17:31.285 --> 00:17:35.700
Is that happened last night?
A moment of weakness?


00:17:35.735 --> 00:17:38.365
No.


00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:43.100
- Did you talk to you ex-wife?
- You think that's what makes me drink.


00:17:43.135 --> 00:17:47.065
- Do you drink when you work?
- No.


00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:50.600
- So then you drink when you get home.
- I have two drinks.


00:17:50.635 --> 00:17:54.765
- Did you had two drinks last night?
- No.


00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:57.565
- And did you talk to your ex-wife?
- I talk to her every night.


00:17:57.600 --> 00:18:03.200
- And did you speak with her last night?
- Are you sensing a breakthrough?


00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:13.600
Do you drink, when you're
involved in a serious crime?


00:18:13.635 --> 00:18:15.865
- No.
- Because?


00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:19.700
- It would be unprofessional.
- So you stop.


00:18:19.735 --> 00:18:23.365
- Yes.
- As long as you need to.


00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:26.800
- Yes.
- And how long do you need to?


00:18:26.835 --> 00:18:30.017
- It depends.
- On what?


00:18:30.052 --> 00:18:33.200
On how long I need to.


00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:39.400
If you've got nothing to do,
pal, find something to do.


00:18:39.435 --> 00:18:44.800
If it's not important,
make it important.


00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:05.150
Rose, where do we keep
the unsolved cases?


00:19:05.185 --> 00:19:07.700
You mean where do "I" keep
the unsolved cases?


00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:11.400
- What kind of cases?
- I want a homicide.


00:19:11.435 --> 00:19:16.200
There's three. 1905, 1923, and 1992.


00:19:16.235 --> 00:19:17.865
- You know?
- Yes...


00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:22.200
- How do you know?
- I'm the dispatcher, I know everything.


00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:27.400
Molly rearranged my files,
I rearrenged them back.


00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:30.265
1992.


00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:34.000
- You said you wanted to get in the field.
- Not in this field...


00:19:34.035 --> 00:19:36.565
- And you're sure you can find it.
- I'm sure...


00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:40.159
No other customers, just, uh, the bank guard...


00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:42.660
...Hasty Hathaway, and the bankteller.


00:19:42.735 --> 00:19:46.200
A robber takes the teller hostage,
uses her as a shield.


00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:48.096
The bank guard gets off
an errant shot...


00:19:48.097 --> 00:19:51.256
... as he's dragging her out
the door. Then they disappear.


00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:54.865
You know, in six months,
none of this is gonna be here,


00:19:54.900 --> 00:19:57.700
some guy bought up the whole point,
gonna put up forty houses...


00:19:57.735 --> 00:20:00.217
- Yeah, rich people from Boston...
- Do me a favor...


00:20:00.252 --> 00:20:02.700
Tell the town council not to
reassess and raise my taxes


00:20:02.735 --> 00:20:05.165
A tenuous relationship at best.


00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:08.200
Ever since our friend Hasty resigned.
They don't seem to understand...


00:20:08.235 --> 00:20:10.267
...why I was hired to begin with...


00:20:10.302 --> 00:20:12.265
but I will tell them just the same.


00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:16.900
Anyway, two years later some hunters find
the teller's body in her shallow grave.


00:20:16.935 --> 00:20:19.900
- Why are you so sure you can find it?
- It would be hard to forget.


00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:21.232
Because?


00:20:21.233 --> 00:20:25.433
I threw up all over the body,
first time I saw her.


00:20:25.468 --> 00:20:27.500
Well, that would be a reason.


00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.500
I'll have a cappucino.


00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:55.100
I threw up the first time
I found a body.


00:20:55.135 --> 00:20:56.965
That's comforting.


00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:59.600
And that's when Lou pulled you out of field?


00:20:59.635 --> 00:21:02.200
Yeah, well, he promoted me to dispatcher...


00:21:02.235 --> 00:21:04.700
- And this is the spot.
- Yeah.


00:21:04.735 --> 00:21:05.765
How you know?


00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:08.500
This is the rock I sat on after I threw up.


00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:14.600
- This about the right depth?
- Yeah.


00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:19.500
Oh my God! The grave is empty!


00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:24.600
Maybe that's because the body
was removed thirteen years ago.


00:21:24.635 --> 00:21:26.965
Jesse, what are we doing?


00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:30.200
We're waiting for a clue to pop up.


00:21:30.300 --> 00:21:35.265
We had this coroner in L.A.,
with that asian guy


00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:40.500
he recovered this body in her shallow grave,
just kept saying "Dig deeper! Dig deeper!"


00:21:40.535 --> 00:21:41.965
Because he was asian?


00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:44.265
No. Because he was stubborn.


00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:47.600
And anytime some would ask "why",
like you keep doing...


00:21:47.635 --> 00:21:50.100
...he'd say "because I'm a
stubborn asian guy".


00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:52.900
Why?


00:21:54.400 --> 00:21:57.400
That's not the point.
The point is...


00:21:57.435 --> 00:22:00.600
...he dug up the murder weapon.


00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:13.300
That was sloppy police work, Lou.


00:22:21.300 --> 00:22:22.900
Thank you.


00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:27.300
- She's afraid of me.
- Oh, she'll be okay.


00:22:27.900 --> 00:22:30.700
- Can I talk to her?
- She won't talk to you, Luther.


00:22:30.735 --> 00:22:33.165
- Because?
- Because she's afraid of you.


00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:36.400
- D'Angelo!
- So Luther, do you remember anything?


00:22:39.200 --> 00:22:42.300
I remember cookies.


00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:46.750
And I remember juice.
Cranberry juice.


00:22:46.785 --> 00:22:50.000
You were shot at the market, Luther.


00:22:50.900 --> 00:22:52.800
Oh.


00:22:54.900 --> 00:22:57.600
Anything new on the drug case, Lou?


00:22:57.700 --> 00:22:59.100
Excuse me?


00:23:00.800 --> 00:23:03.900
Anything new on the drug case?


00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:08.000
Not really.


00:23:22.400 --> 00:23:24.365
And no blood at the scene.


00:23:24.400 --> 00:23:26.365
Apparently not.
There is nothin in the report...


00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:29.800
No, a lot of things are in the report.
I know you're fond of your old boss...


00:23:29.835 --> 00:23:33.065
...but that report is a mess.
And what was the robber wearing?


00:23:33.100 --> 00:23:35.426
Jesse, I know these are
the robber's clothes.


00:23:35.427 --> 00:23:36.927
He didn't need the hostage anymore...


00:23:36.935 --> 00:23:40.700
...so he shot the teller, buried in a
shallow grave, changed his own clothes...


00:23:40.735 --> 00:23:42.565
...buried them, so he
wouldn't be recognized.


00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:45.200
Well, actually he buried his clothes,
and then he buried the teller...


00:23:45.235 --> 00:23:46.765
...doesn't it seem backwards to you?


00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:49.465
- I guess it could be...
- Lou should've found these.


00:23:49.500 --> 00:23:53.300
- He found the body, that's pretty big.
- Actually some hunter's found the body.


00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:56.665
And what d'you suppose
made these holes?


00:23:56.700 --> 00:24:00.000
- Ugh, fifteen years underground?
- Organic matter.


00:24:00.035 --> 00:24:03.200
How was the body ID-d?


00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:07.265
- Her mother.
- Not even dental records?


00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:12.300
"Mary Lewis came in, looked to the
body, and said 'that's my little girl' ".


00:24:14.500 --> 00:24:17.000
Excuse me.


00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:23.600
- I'm Chief Stone.
- My name's Sam Holton.


00:24:23.635 --> 00:24:26.200
My daughter Cathleen.


00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:32.000
Why don't we go on into my office.
Officer Gammon.


00:24:34.800 --> 00:24:38.000
We'd just passed Paradise Cove
when it happened.


00:24:38.035 --> 00:24:41.200
On one of those yachts
come up for Raceweek.


00:24:41.235 --> 00:24:42.817
What happened?


00:24:42.852 --> 00:24:44.400
I was raped.


00:24:45.200 --> 00:24:47.900
- Do you know who did it?
- The owner of the boat.


00:24:48.100 --> 00:24:51.700
- Do you know the name of the boat?
- The "Lady Jane".


00:24:51.735 --> 00:24:55.265
- Could you pick the owner out of a lineup?
- Yeah.


00:24:55.300 --> 00:25:00.200
Good. Officer Gammon will take the rest
of your report and then we'll look into it.


00:25:00.235 --> 00:25:02.500
Now if you excuse me...


00:25:06.500 --> 00:25:09.700
- Have you talked to your wife?
- Ex-wife.


00:25:10.400 --> 00:25:14.200
I'll take that as a "no".
I thought you spoke to her every night.


00:25:14.235 --> 00:25:17.065
- Not lately.
- Why not?


00:25:17.100 --> 00:25:20.600
- She's seeing someone.
- At night?


00:25:20.635 --> 00:25:23.065
- Yes.
- At your house?


00:25:23.100 --> 00:25:27.400
- Oh, yeah.
- How do you feel about that?


00:25:27.435 --> 00:25:31.300
Like I wanna kill him.


00:25:38.400 --> 00:25:43.900
Do you imagine her
with him, having sex?


00:25:47.200 --> 00:25:48.500
Yes.


00:25:49.200 --> 00:25:52.265
- Does she tell you about it?
- No.


00:25:52.300 --> 00:25:54.800
- So, in fact, you don't know
what she's doing.


00:25:54.835 --> 00:25:59.000
I don't know anything...


00:26:04.300 --> 00:26:07.400
So you invent it.


00:26:08.300 --> 00:26:11.900
How long have you been
inventing her life?


00:26:14.100 --> 00:26:18.300
- I'll take that as an "always".
- Not always.


00:26:18.700 --> 00:26:25.200
- Since the divorce?
- You're pretty good at this.


00:26:25.600 --> 00:26:28.700
How many year's it to
take to be a psychiatrist?


00:26:28.735 --> 00:26:31.800
- Ten.
- You got to go at medical school first.


00:26:32.900 --> 00:26:37.000
- I'd have a question for you.
- A medical question?


00:26:37.300 --> 00:26:43.300
- A medical slash-cop question.
- Is this important?


00:26:43.700 --> 00:26:45.600
I hope so.


00:26:45.900 --> 00:26:47.765
What's the question?


00:26:47.800 --> 00:26:51.200
Bugs go after organic
matter first, right?


00:26:51.600 --> 00:26:55.465
What kind of bugs?
What kind of organic matter?


00:26:55.500 --> 00:26:59.465
I have these clothes, and they've
been buried for about fifteen years...


00:26:59.500 --> 00:27:04.800
...and pretty deteriorated, but there
are two big holes - one on the shirt...


00:27:04.835 --> 00:27:10.100
...one on the jacket, and they
line up, with, I think it might be, blood.


00:27:10.600 --> 00:27:16.200
You know what I think?
I think you won't be drinking tonight.


00:27:31.400 --> 00:27:33.200
Who are you lookin' at?


00:27:53.300 --> 00:27:59.500
<i>Hi, jesse. It's Jenn. I guess you
already left. I'll call you at the office.</i>


00:28:02.800 --> 00:28:09.600
<i>Hi, jesse. It's Jenn. I guess you
already left. I'll call you at the office..</i>


00:29:04.700 --> 00:29:08.500
- So where is Stone?
- Town Council.


00:29:08.900 --> 00:29:12.400
- You interviewed the raped victim?
- Basically.


00:29:12.435 --> 00:29:15.865
- Don't you think he should've
been there? I mean...


00:29:15.900 --> 00:29:21.100
He's always the first one to work.
But he wasn't the other day.


00:29:21.135 --> 00:29:24.300
- That's correct.
- Why do you think that is?


00:29:25.800 --> 00:29:27.700
- You know what I think?
- Tony.


00:29:28.300 --> 00:29:30.500
I don't really care what you think.


00:29:31.300 --> 00:29:36.300
The rabid skunk is no longer a threat,
Officer D'Angelo expressed his regrets.


00:29:36.335 --> 00:29:39.865
Uh, sixty-three parking tickets,
fourteen traffic stops...


00:29:39.900 --> 00:29:43.700
...and Edwin claims the Civil War
Memorial has been vandalized.


00:29:43.735 --> 00:29:45.465
You don't think it has been?


00:29:45.500 --> 00:29:49.050
Maybe you could tell him
he's watering too much.


00:29:49.085 --> 00:29:52.600
- What about this rape case?
- What about it?


00:29:52.635 --> 00:29:55.465
- Anyone arrested?
- No.


00:29:55.500 --> 00:29:57.665
- Good...
- Rape out of season?


00:29:57.700 --> 00:30:00.765
All our merchants need Raceweek,
I don't need a scandal.


00:30:00.800 --> 00:30:01.877
I know that.


00:30:01.878 --> 00:30:04.478
The Fall Regatta brings in
a lot of revenue.


00:30:04.535 --> 00:30:07.100
Including your paycheck.


00:30:08.900 --> 00:30:12.900
- So how have you been?
- Fine.


00:30:12.935 --> 00:30:15.800
- No problems.
- No.


00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:20.000
No... personal issues?


00:30:22.900 --> 00:30:25.265
Anything we need to know about?


00:30:25.300 --> 00:30:30.100
Yes, my deputy doesn't want you to
reassess her house and raise her taxes.


00:30:45.900 --> 00:30:47.865
What are you looking at?


00:30:47.900 --> 00:30:51.600
I was admiring the rigging
on the "Lady Jane".


00:30:52.900 --> 00:30:55.065
What d'you use for bait?


00:30:55.100 --> 00:30:58.450
Bugs, worms, last night supper.


00:30:58.485 --> 00:31:01.800
- Catch much?
- Don't catch spit.


00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:02.800
- Plenty of fish, though.
- Yep.


00:31:05.800 --> 00:31:10.400
- Maybe you should just shoot 'em.
- The fish or the bank robber?


00:31:14.700 --> 00:31:16.300
You a good shot, Bob?


00:31:16.600 --> 00:31:17.700
I was certified


00:31:18.200 --> 00:31:20.600
expert with a pistol
in the Army.


00:31:20.700 --> 00:31:21.500
Which war?


00:31:21.800 --> 00:31:22.200
Korea.


00:31:23.500 --> 00:31:25.100
You a good shot now?


00:31:25.135 --> 00:31:26.100
I don't know.


00:31:26.800 --> 00:31:28.400
How old are you, Bob?


00:31:28.900 --> 00:31:29.500
76.


00:31:31.000 --> 00:31:33.600
You a good shot
when you were 61?


00:31:34.100 --> 00:31:35.300
I thought I was.


00:31:35.900 --> 00:31:39.300
You had to be qualified
to be a bank guard.


00:31:40.500 --> 00:31:44.600
Have you ever been in a hostage
situation, Chief Stone?


00:31:47.800 --> 00:31:48.400
Yes.


00:31:50.900 --> 00:31:52.600
Did you take the shot?


00:31:55.400 --> 00:31:56.000
Yes.


00:31:56.700 --> 00:31:57.400
So did I.


00:31:58.600 --> 00:32:02.300
I reached for my backup,
and I went to the door.


00:32:02.400 --> 00:32:04.600
I saw him in
my front sight.


00:32:05.700 --> 00:32:09.700
I figured he'd kill Rebecca
when he didn't need her.


00:32:10.500 --> 00:32:12.600
Well, you figured right, Bob.


00:32:13.000 --> 00:32:15.600
What caliber bullet
killed Rebecca?


00:32:19.700 --> 00:32:20.300
.38.


00:32:20.600 --> 00:32:22.700
That's what I was shooting.


00:32:23.300 --> 00:32:25.200
You don't think that I...


00:32:27.400 --> 00:32:30.000
No. And I don't
think you should.


00:32:32.700 --> 00:32:33.600
Why is that?


00:32:33.700 --> 00:32:36.300
Not healthy.
It will drive you to drink.


00:32:36.400 --> 00:32:37.300
Already did.


00:32:38.200 --> 00:32:40.400
Six years sober come December.


00:32:46.400 --> 00:32:48.200
And when did this happen?


00:32:48.235 --> 00:32:49.000
Four days ago.


00:32:49.100 --> 00:32:51.600
Cathleen, we have
no evidence of that.


00:32:51.700 --> 00:32:53.000
So you think I was lying?


00:32:53.100 --> 00:32:54.500
It doesn't mean you' re lying.


00:32:54.600 --> 00:32:56.200
It just means
there was no sperm.


00:32:56.300 --> 00:32:58.200
He was wearing
a rubber.


00:32:58.800 --> 00:33:01.600
I thought it was be best
if Cathleen


00:33:01.900 --> 00:33:03.200
and I discussed this.


00:33:03.300 --> 00:33:04.300
The rape test was inconclusive.


00:33:04.400 --> 00:33:07.200
Why don't you tell us the part
you didn't want your dad


00:33:07.300 --> 00:33:08.600
to hear, Cathleen?


00:33:09.900 --> 00:33:12.100
They made me do a striptease.


00:33:12.500 --> 00:33:13.400
Were you drinking?


00:33:13.500 --> 00:33:16.600
Yes. They said
I had to do a striptease


00:33:17.200 --> 00:33:19.600
or they wouldn't
take me back to shore.


00:33:19.700 --> 00:33:20.400
Who is they?


00:33:20.500 --> 00:33:23.300
The guy that raped me
and two other guys.


00:33:23.400 --> 00:33:25.300
They said
I had to strip.


00:33:25.400 --> 00:33:26.400
So you' re saying
they forced you?


00:33:26.500 --> 00:33:30.700
Yes. And then the guy who owned
the boat took me downstairs.


00:33:30.800 --> 00:33:33.000
I thought, you know, so
I could get dressed again,


00:33:33.100 --> 00:33:35.500
but he just threw me on the bed
and raped me.


00:33:35.600 --> 00:33:36.500
He was like an animal.


00:33:36.600 --> 00:33:38.200
Just threw me down
and jumped on me.


00:33:38.300 --> 00:33:39.900
But he wore a condom.


00:33:40.000 --> 00:33:40.465
Yes.


00:33:40.500 --> 00:33:44.300
Did he put that on just before
he jumped on you like an animal?


00:33:44.400 --> 00:33:45.700
Yeah. Just before.


00:33:46.400 --> 00:33:47.900
Was it in a packet?


00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:48.565
Yes.


00:33:48.600 --> 00:33:50.100
Did he have to open the packet?


00:33:50.200 --> 00:33:51.500
I don't remember.


00:33:58.600 --> 00:34:01.000
You think she's lying?
You don't think she was raped?


00:34:01.100 --> 00:34:02.300
I didn't say that.
Well, I think


00:34:02.400 --> 00:34:04.500
we can get a warrant.
Sure, we can get a warrant,


00:34:04.600 --> 00:34:05.700
but I don't want to.


00:34:05.800 --> 00:34:06.700
Since when
do you care


00:34:06.800 --> 00:34:07.700
what the Town
Council thinks?


00:34:07.800 --> 00:34:09.800
I don't.
But I do care about Paradise.


00:34:09.900 --> 00:34:12.000
You prosecute a rape case
in a resort town,


00:34:12.100 --> 00:34:14.100
all the cable news channels


00:34:14.200 --> 00:34:15.100
will live here.


00:34:15.200 --> 00:34:17.700
And no rape shield law
will protect that kid.


00:34:17.800 --> 00:34:19.300
Legally, she's not a kid.


00:34:19.400 --> 00:34:21.900
I think it's blood
on his clothes.


00:34:22.000 --> 00:34:22.800
Excuse me?


00:34:23.800 --> 00:34:27.400
I want to test
the robber's clothes for blood.


00:34:27.700 --> 00:34:30.000
So, after he
shot the teller,


00:34:30.600 --> 00:34:32.100
he dragged the body
to the grave


00:34:32.200 --> 00:34:33.400
and got blood on
his clothes. So what?


00:34:33.500 --> 00:34:36.600
So what? How much money
was taken in the robbery?


00:34:36.700 --> 00:34:39.700
Just the cash
that was in the bank: $24,000.


00:34:39.800 --> 00:34:40.900
Hardly worth a life.


00:34:41.000 --> 00:34:41.900
Jesse, what's the point?


00:34:42.000 --> 00:34:45.100
The point is, this isn't
just a robbery, Officer Gammon.


00:34:45.200 --> 00:34:46.300
It's a murder.


00:34:46.800 --> 00:34:48.200
And the guy got away with it.


00:34:48.300 --> 00:34:51.300
This report doesn't even
say whether she was shot


00:34:51.400 --> 00:34:52.900
from the front or the back.


00:34:53.000 --> 00:34:53.700
No, it doesn't.


00:34:53.800 --> 00:34:55.400
And I'm not happy
with the ID of the body.


00:34:55.500 --> 00:34:57.300
You don't want to run a DNA test.
I do.


00:34:57.400 --> 00:35:00.000
You don't think a mother could
recognize her own daughter?!


00:35:00.100 --> 00:35:01.700
Not after two years underground.


00:35:01.800 --> 00:35:03.500
She recognized the clothes.


00:35:03.600 --> 00:35:04.700
And where are they?


00:35:04.800 --> 00:35:05.700
Lieu returned


00:35:06.500 --> 00:35:07.700
the effects
to the family.


00:35:07.800 --> 00:35:09.400
Jesse, this stuff
isn't important!


00:35:09.500 --> 00:35:11.200
I think it is.
Why?


00:35:11.235 --> 00:35:12.900
Because I need it to be!


00:35:28.400 --> 00:35:31.700
What was the mother's
last known whereabouts?


00:35:31.800 --> 00:35:34.500
Sisters of Mercy
Hospital, up north.


00:35:34.900 --> 00:35:36.000
Jesse...


00:35:36.400 --> 00:35:38.600
I think DeAngelo went
to the Town Council.


00:35:38.700 --> 00:35:41.000
I would expect no less of him.


00:35:43.200 --> 00:35:44.800
They' re laying for you.


00:35:44.900 --> 00:35:46.000
The ugly truth of it, Rose,


00:35:46.100 --> 00:35:48.600
is it doesn't matter
a whole hell of a lot to me.


00:35:48.700 --> 00:35:52.300
Jesse, you need to concentrate
on the rape case.


00:35:57.900 --> 00:35:58.800
I know.


00:35:59.600 --> 00:36:00.700
You' re right.


00:36:01.900 --> 00:36:02.700
Thank you.


00:37:17.400 --> 00:37:18.000
Yes?


00:37:18.800 --> 00:37:21.500
I'm Jesse Stone,
the police chief in Paradise.


00:37:21.600 --> 00:37:23.700
You' re a long way from home.


00:37:23.800 --> 00:37:26.000
I was looking for Mary Lewis.


00:37:26.700 --> 00:37:28.300
Oh, my mom's resting.


00:37:29.300 --> 00:37:31.200
You look like your sister.


00:37:31.500 --> 00:37:33.400
Is this is about Rebecca?


00:37:34.600 --> 00:37:35.200
Yes.


00:37:35.800 --> 00:37:37.500
Oh, I'm... I'm sorry.


00:37:37.900 --> 00:37:39.900
I'm Leeann Lewis. Come in.


00:37:40.300 --> 00:37:41.100
Thank you.


00:37:50.000 --> 00:37:53.400
You can speak to her,
but she won't speak back.


00:37:53.500 --> 00:37:55.100
My mom had a stroke.


00:37:56.600 --> 00:37:57.800
Mama, this is...


00:37:59.300 --> 00:38:01.100
Jesse Stone,
Mrs. Lewis.


00:38:01.700 --> 00:38:03.100
I was just visiting


00:38:03.500 --> 00:38:04.400
with Leeann.


00:38:07.800 --> 00:38:09.800
Would you like some coffee?


00:38:11.200 --> 00:38:12.100
I would.


00:38:14.400 --> 00:38:16.600
Nice meeting you,
Mrs. Lewis.


00:38:25.300 --> 00:38:27.100
When did your mom
have the stroke?


00:38:27.200 --> 00:38:29.500
The day after she
identified Rebecca.


00:38:29.600 --> 00:38:32.000
Thank you for
not upsetting her.


00:38:32.300 --> 00:38:34.700
I assume you have
power of attorney.


00:38:34.800 --> 00:38:37.200
I thought this
case was closed.


00:38:37.500 --> 00:38:38.600
No. Just cold.


00:38:40.300 --> 00:38:42.100
What do you want, Chief Stone?


00:38:42.200 --> 00:38:43.900
Probably what you want.


00:38:44.400 --> 00:38:45.600
Justice for your sister.


00:38:45.700 --> 00:38:48.000
I'd like permissión
to exhume


00:38:48.300 --> 00:38:49.000
the body.


00:38:49.600 --> 00:38:51.300
My sister was cremated.


00:38:53.800 --> 00:38:54.400
Okay.


00:38:56.300 --> 00:38:57.000
This is old.


00:38:57.100 --> 00:38:58.700
I'm going to get
you a new pot.


00:38:58.800 --> 00:39:00.300
Did you see your
sister's body?


00:39:00.400 --> 00:39:04.100
No. Maybe my mother
wouldn't have had her stroke


00:39:04.900 --> 00:39:05.800
if I had been here.


00:39:05.900 --> 00:39:08.000
I wouldn't beat yourself up.


00:39:08.400 --> 00:39:10.700
You've obviously devoted
yourself to her.


00:39:10.800 --> 00:39:12.600
I left my job in L.A.,


00:39:13.000 --> 00:39:15.600
and I got her out
of that hospital,


00:39:15.700 --> 00:39:17.600
and we've been here ever since.


00:39:17.700 --> 00:39:19.400
Long way from Paradise.


00:39:21.500 --> 00:39:22.800
Too many memories.


00:39:24.300 --> 00:39:25.400
Do you have any


00:39:25.500 --> 00:39:28.600
personal effects of
your sister? Pictures?


00:39:28.800 --> 00:39:29.400
Why?


00:39:29.600 --> 00:39:31.000
Well, it's just
the way I work.


00:39:31.100 --> 00:39:32.400
Gives me a sense
of the person.


00:39:32.500 --> 00:39:33.600
Frankly, there's
not much in our files.


00:39:33.700 --> 00:39:37.700
We really don't want to open old
wounds unless there's a reason.


00:39:37.800 --> 00:39:40.000
Oh, I think there's a reason.


00:39:40.700 --> 00:39:44.700
Well, I got rid of all that
stuff after the funeral.


00:39:44.800 --> 00:39:46.700
It upset your mom?
Yeah.


00:39:48.600 --> 00:39:50.500
Frankly, it upset me, too.


00:39:52.900 --> 00:39:53.700
I'm sorry.


00:39:56.600 --> 00:39:58.500
This is going
to take a while.


00:39:58.600 --> 00:40:01.500
Do you still want coffee,
Chief Stone?


00:40:01.900 --> 00:40:02.600
Jesse.


00:40:03.700 --> 00:40:04.400
Jesse.


00:40:04.800 --> 00:40:06.400
Coffee would be good.


00:40:07.500 --> 00:40:09.200
It's a long way back.


00:40:21.800 --> 00:40:22.500
Jesse?


00:40:24.300 --> 00:40:26.200
Would you like
to eat at the bar?


00:40:26.300 --> 00:40:27.200
Sure, Laura.


00:40:28.200 --> 00:40:28.900
Okay.


00:40:32.400 --> 00:40:33.800
I thought I'd stop by,


00:40:33.900 --> 00:40:34.900
see if you need any help
fighting crime.


00:40:35.000 --> 00:40:38.800
What's happening at home
that you'd rather be here?


00:40:38.900 --> 00:40:39.800
Nothing.


00:40:40.100 --> 00:40:41.000
Not nothing.


00:40:42.600 --> 00:40:46.500
My wife's younger brother
is visiting with his wife.


00:40:47.700 --> 00:40:49.500
They have young children.


00:40:49.800 --> 00:40:52.400
You don't care
for young children?


00:40:52.500 --> 00:40:53.800
Neither of us do.


00:40:54.000 --> 00:40:55.600
But it's her brother.


00:40:55.700 --> 00:40:59.400
So your dropping by is not
all about helping me.


00:40:59.700 --> 00:41:01.200
It's nothing about that.


00:41:01.300 --> 00:41:02.600
Are you staying for dinner?


00:41:02.700 --> 00:41:05.300
Can I tell my wife
it's business?


00:41:05.500 --> 00:41:08.700
You can if you crank up
your lab for me.


00:41:09.200 --> 00:41:10.900
There's something
I want you to check.


00:41:11.000 --> 00:41:12.900
Can't Doc Perkins do it?


00:41:13.400 --> 00:41:16.200
I don't want to destroy
his confidence.


00:41:16.300 --> 00:41:19.300
Yeah, but State Homicide
operates on a budget.


00:41:19.400 --> 00:41:21.000
This stuff costs money.


00:41:21.100 --> 00:41:22.100
Is it important?


00:41:22.200 --> 00:41:23.400
I have no idea.


00:41:26.600 --> 00:41:28.900
Will you call
my wife for me?


00:41:30.100 --> 00:41:30.700
Okay.


00:41:32.600 --> 00:41:34.700
Then I'll crank up the lab.


00:41:36.900 --> 00:41:39.600
You know, marriage
is hard for cops.


00:41:39.700 --> 00:41:42.300
And the only people
we know how to talk to


00:41:42.400 --> 00:41:44.100
are the women we marry.


00:41:44.900 --> 00:41:47.000
Then the marriage breaks up,


00:41:47.100 --> 00:41:49.500
and you need to talk to someone,


00:41:49.700 --> 00:41:51.600
and only one you can't talk to


00:41:51.700 --> 00:41:53.600
is the woman you married.


00:41:53.900 --> 00:41:55.700
When did Molly call you?


00:41:57.800 --> 00:42:00.400
The morning
after you woke her up.


00:42:02.100 --> 00:42:05.500
Oh, Captain Healy will be
joining me for dinner, Laura.


00:42:05.600 --> 00:42:07.300
What can I get for you?


00:42:07.400 --> 00:42:09.000
Scotch on the rocks...


00:42:09.700 --> 00:42:11.200
and another for the Chief.


00:42:11.300 --> 00:42:12.500
I'm good, Laura.


00:42:26.000 --> 00:42:29.000
Have you talked
to the son of a bitch?


00:42:29.300 --> 00:42:29.900
No.


00:42:30.300 --> 00:42:33.600
But I will be talking
to the son of a bitch.


00:42:33.700 --> 00:42:34.600
Why'd Cathleen drop out


00:42:34.700 --> 00:42:37.600
of high school
before her senior year?


00:42:39.700 --> 00:42:42.700
What's that have to do
with her being raped?


00:42:42.800 --> 00:42:43.800
I don't know.


00:42:45.900 --> 00:42:48.600
I tried, but
she just wouldn't go.


00:42:48.900 --> 00:42:50.600
And I couldn't make her.


00:42:50.700 --> 00:42:51.900
I work all day.


00:42:52.300 --> 00:42:53.300
Her mom is...


00:42:53.400 --> 00:42:54.000
Gone.


00:42:54.800 --> 00:42:58.600
Took off with a guy
when Cathleen was just six...


00:43:00.500 --> 00:43:01.200
Look...


00:43:03.200 --> 00:43:04.900
I'm sorry, Chief Stone.


00:43:05.300 --> 00:43:07.900
This whole thing's
just got me...


00:43:08.800 --> 00:43:09.600
Pissed off?


00:43:14.200 --> 00:43:16.000
She came home very late.


00:43:18.000 --> 00:43:19.300
I confronted her.


00:43:20.500 --> 00:43:24.400
She got real upset,
and then it all just came out.


00:43:25.700 --> 00:43:27.800
Well, two things
you need to know.


00:43:27.900 --> 00:43:29.900
One is, I'm going to talk
to the son of a bitch.


00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:34.400
And two, you' re going to stay
away from the son of a bitch.


00:43:34.500 --> 00:43:35.400
Because?


00:43:35.900 --> 00:43:38.100
Because I'm the police chief.


00:44:04.400 --> 00:44:06.100
What were you thinking?


00:44:11.500 --> 00:44:12.200
Jesse!


00:44:14.800 --> 00:44:17.100
Boy, I do not get
many visitors.


00:44:17.200 --> 00:44:18.200
So how you doing, Hasty?


00:44:18.300 --> 00:44:21.100
Don't say "How you doing?"
to a convict.


00:44:21.200 --> 00:44:22.800
Okay, how's it going?


00:44:22.900 --> 00:44:26.100
Well, I teach
illiterate prisoners to read.


00:44:27.300 --> 00:44:30.200
I give financial advice
to the guards.


00:44:30.400 --> 00:44:32.100
How's the drinking thing?


00:44:32.200 --> 00:44:34.300
Better since I gave up hope.


00:44:35.900 --> 00:44:37.000
How's my wife?


00:44:38.200 --> 00:44:39.300
Ex-wife, Hasty.


00:44:39.900 --> 00:44:41.700
How's she doing?
Cissy?


00:44:41.800 --> 00:44:42.700
Is... Cissy.


00:44:43.800 --> 00:44:45.000
But she's okay?


00:44:46.800 --> 00:44:47.400
Yes.


00:44:47.700 --> 00:44:49.400
Jesse, you and Cissy...


00:44:52.300 --> 00:44:53.200
You never...


00:44:53.800 --> 00:44:54.800
No. We never.


00:44:59.100 --> 00:45:00.500
So, no hard feelings?


00:45:00.600 --> 00:45:02.500
Hey, a guy saves your life.


00:45:02.600 --> 00:45:04.900
Albeit for the wrong reasons...


00:45:05.900 --> 00:45:07.700
What are you doing here?


00:45:09.500 --> 00:45:11.700
Your bank was robbed in 1992.


00:45:12.800 --> 00:45:14.100
Teller was killed.


00:45:14.300 --> 00:45:15.700
Yeah, Rebecca. Nice kid.


00:45:15.800 --> 00:45:17.700
What do you remember about it?


00:45:17.800 --> 00:45:18.265
Nothing.


00:45:18.300 --> 00:45:20.900
Hasty, you can't be
put away twice


00:45:21.000 --> 00:45:21.900
for money laundering.


00:45:22.000 --> 00:45:23.000
I know that.
So?


00:45:23.100 --> 00:45:25.000
So I just didn't see anything.
Because?


00:45:25.100 --> 00:45:28.900
Because I was hiding
under my desk the whole time.


00:45:29.400 --> 00:45:33.000
There were no surveillance
cameras in your bank.


00:45:33.800 --> 00:45:34.600
Small town.


00:45:35.000 --> 00:45:37.400
Were you laundering money
for Gino Fish back then?


00:45:37.500 --> 00:45:38.400
No.


00:45:40.900 --> 00:45:43.000
No, on my sacred honor, no.


00:45:46.500 --> 00:45:49.100
You know, Hasty, when I
said you saved my life,


00:45:49.200 --> 00:45:52.400
I wasn't talking about the night
I arrested you.


00:45:52.500 --> 00:45:56.100
I meant you saved my life
because you hired me.


00:45:57.000 --> 00:45:58.800
Albeit for the wrong reasons.


00:45:58.900 --> 00:46:01.100
I'm very fond of you, Jesse.


00:46:04.200 --> 00:46:05.300
See you, Hasty.


00:46:17.500 --> 00:46:18.100
Suit.


00:46:18.500 --> 00:46:19.100
Jesse!


00:46:19.700 --> 00:46:21.000
Where have you
been, Skipper?


00:46:21.100 --> 00:46:21.800
Fighting crime.


00:46:21.900 --> 00:46:24.200
Rose at the
orthodontist again?


00:46:24.800 --> 00:46:25.400
Yes.


00:46:26.500 --> 00:46:27.600
How you feeling?


00:46:27.700 --> 00:46:28.365
Perfect.


00:46:28.400 --> 00:46:30.300
You lost a little weight.


00:46:31.600 --> 00:46:32.800
I'm not much good


00:46:32.900 --> 00:46:34.100
with the phones.


00:46:34.800 --> 00:46:35.900
You supposed to be here?


00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:37.100
They let me out of the hospital.


00:46:37.200 --> 00:46:39.700
They say it was okay for you
to go back to work?


00:46:39.800 --> 00:46:40.500
I didn't ask.


00:46:40.600 --> 00:46:43.500
Well, I need you
to answer the phones


00:46:44.600 --> 00:46:45.900
for now, Suitcase.


00:46:46.000 --> 00:46:48.100
How do you feel about that?


00:46:48.400 --> 00:46:49.700
I don't like it.


00:46:50.000 --> 00:46:51.400
I feel fine, Lieu.


00:46:53.300 --> 00:46:53.900
Okay.


00:47:03.300 --> 00:47:05.200
Boy, that thing's a mess.


00:47:05.700 --> 00:47:06.400
Tell me about it.


00:47:06.500 --> 00:47:08.300
The folder's torn.
The pictures are dirty.


00:47:08.400 --> 00:47:09.400
The papers are all wrinkled...


00:47:09.500 --> 00:47:11.200
Well, I threw it
across the room.


00:47:11.300 --> 00:47:12.300
Why'd you do that?


00:47:12.400 --> 00:47:14.000
Because it's a mess.


00:47:16.800 --> 00:47:18.900
I think DeAngelo wants your job.


00:47:19.000 --> 00:47:20.300
I feel it in my cells.


00:47:20.400 --> 00:47:21.600
Well, actually, he thinks


00:47:21.700 --> 00:47:24.600
he should have had the job
to begin with.


00:47:24.700 --> 00:47:27.000
I'd like to help you
with your drug case.


00:47:27.100 --> 00:47:31.800
Suit, do you remember anything
about your stay at the hospital?


00:47:32.300 --> 00:47:32.900
No.


00:47:33.700 --> 00:47:34.200
Okay...


00:47:34.700 --> 00:47:36.900
What did you think
about the bank robbery?


00:47:37.000 --> 00:47:38.100
I think you' re on to something.


00:47:38.200 --> 00:47:39.600
Rose doesn't think so.


00:47:39.700 --> 00:47:41.500
Rose hasn't been in the field.


00:47:41.600 --> 00:47:43.000
Well, she threw up.


00:47:43.300 --> 00:47:44.300
Was she sick?


00:47:44.700 --> 00:47:46.100
It's not important.


00:47:46.600 --> 00:47:49.900
You know, I think
we should check for blood


00:47:50.300 --> 00:47:52.400
on those clothes
you found.


00:47:52.700 --> 00:47:56.800
You know, there might be
an upside to this coma thing.


00:47:57.400 --> 00:47:58.500
What are you talking about?


00:47:58.600 --> 00:48:01.000
You know what I'm talking about.


00:48:03.400 --> 00:48:04.200
You mean...


00:48:05.600 --> 00:48:06.200
Yes.


00:48:07.300 --> 00:48:08.300
Cop intuition.


00:48:08.600 --> 00:48:10.900
Now you' re as crazy as I am.


00:48:22.700 --> 00:48:23.900
Watch your step.


00:48:29.400 --> 00:48:31.100
Well... Inspector Yokel.


00:48:31.900 --> 00:48:33.800
Actually it's Chief Yokel.


00:48:34.900 --> 00:48:35.800
Where's your badge?


00:48:35.900 --> 00:48:37.300
It's in a drawer.


00:48:37.900 --> 00:48:38.600
Ah...


00:48:39.100 --> 00:48:39.900
This your boat?


00:48:40.000 --> 00:48:42.900
Why, you don't think I could
afford a boat like this?


00:48:43.000 --> 00:48:44.600
The Lady Jane's mine.


00:48:45.400 --> 00:48:46.500
I'm Chief Stone.


00:48:46.600 --> 00:48:48.500
This is Officer Gammon.
I'm Harrison.


00:48:48.600 --> 00:48:50.400
Nice to meet you,
Mr. Harrison.


00:48:50.500 --> 00:48:52.000
Harrison is my first name.


00:48:52.100 --> 00:48:53.300
I'm Harrison Pendleton.


00:48:53.400 --> 00:48:54.000
I see.


00:48:55.100 --> 00:48:55.900
Nice boat.


00:48:56.500 --> 00:48:57.300
Schooner.


00:48:58.400 --> 00:49:02.400
Officer Gammon would like
to ask you a few questions.


00:49:07.300 --> 00:49:09.600
Do you know a Cathleen Holton?


00:49:10.500 --> 00:49:11.100
I do.


00:49:12.200 --> 00:49:14.200
Was she a guest
on your schooner?


00:49:14.300 --> 00:49:15.100
Yes.
When?


00:49:16.300 --> 00:49:17.000
Four days ago.


00:49:17.100 --> 00:49:19.900
She joined some friends and me
for an evening cruise.


00:49:20.000 --> 00:49:21.900
Do you know how old she is?!


00:49:22.000 --> 00:49:24.200
Yes. 18 years and two months.


00:49:25.400 --> 00:49:27.000
She showed me her ID.


00:49:28.700 --> 00:49:31.400
I was wondering
if you could show me below.


00:49:31.500 --> 00:49:33.200
Do you have a warrant?


00:49:33.500 --> 00:49:34.100
No.


00:49:35.600 --> 00:49:36.700
Well, then, no.


00:49:42.000 --> 00:49:43.900
Guy's got two last names.


00:49:44.200 --> 00:49:46.300
You might have briefed me
that I was going


00:49:46.400 --> 00:49:47.500
to question the suspect.


00:49:47.600 --> 00:49:49.400
Well, I'm not sure
he's a suspect.


00:49:49.500 --> 00:49:52.300
But I thought
you handled it well...


00:49:52.400 --> 00:49:54.200
till you got pissed off.


00:49:57.500 --> 00:50:00.000
Jesse, why don't you get
a cell phone?


00:50:00.100 --> 00:50:01.500
' Cause I don't like them.


00:50:01.600 --> 00:50:02.800
You can always page me.


00:50:02.900 --> 00:50:04.100
I have.
Well...


00:50:05.300 --> 00:50:06.900
call me
on the car radio.


00:50:07.000 --> 00:50:07.465
I have.


00:50:07.500 --> 00:50:09.600
You've been spending
a lot of time


00:50:09.700 --> 00:50:11.100
away from the office.


00:50:11.200 --> 00:50:11.900
I have.


00:50:12.300 --> 00:50:12.900
At home?


00:50:14.000 --> 00:50:14.300
No.


00:50:15.900 --> 00:50:16.500
Good.


00:50:18.100 --> 00:50:19.900
So, I assume
you've talked


00:50:20.000 --> 00:50:21.400
to the bank guard.


00:50:22.200 --> 00:50:22.800
I did.


00:50:23.800 --> 00:50:24.900
Have you talked to the mother?


00:50:25.000 --> 00:50:26.400
Actually, I didn't.


00:50:29.400 --> 00:50:30.800
What are you doing?


00:50:44.700 --> 00:50:45.800
Run that plate.


00:51:00.700 --> 00:51:03.100
License and
registration, please.


00:51:05.400 --> 00:51:08.000
Did I do something
wrong, Officer?


00:51:08.300 --> 00:51:10.700
You have no front
license plate,


00:51:11.500 --> 00:51:12.300
Mr. Genest.


00:51:14.400 --> 00:51:15.700
I knew someone named Genest.


00:51:15.800 --> 00:51:16.600
Joe Genest?


00:51:18.000 --> 00:51:18.900
He your brother?


00:51:19.000 --> 00:51:20.400
He was my brother.


00:51:22.900 --> 00:51:23.900
I tell you what.


00:51:24.000 --> 00:51:26.600
I'm going to let you off
on the license plate.


00:51:26.700 --> 00:51:27.800
Just put one on.


00:51:27.900 --> 00:51:29.300
Thank you, Officer.


00:51:29.900 --> 00:51:31.000
One more thing.


00:51:32.800 --> 00:51:35.100
Don't follow me around, Terry.


00:59:46.200 --> 00:59:46.800
Hello.


00:59:47.500 --> 00:59:48.400
Jesse Stone.


00:59:48.500 --> 00:59:49.200
Oh, I, I checked in storage


00:59:49.300 --> 00:59:51.900
and I couldn't find anything
that might help you.


00:59:52.000 --> 00:59:53.000
I'm so sorry.


00:59:55.000 --> 00:59:57.100
It's like she didn't exist.


00:59:58.000 --> 00:59:59.500
Regrets, Chief Stone.


01:00:00.200 --> 01:00:00.800
Jesse.


01:00:02.300 --> 01:00:03.100
Jesse...


01:00:05.200 --> 01:00:08.300
Listen, um...
I know this is forward, um,


01:00:10.300 --> 01:00:12.700
but if you' re ever around here,


01:00:14.700 --> 01:00:15.500
I'd love to see you again.


01:00:15.600 --> 01:00:19.900
Well, if you' re ever in
Paradise, I'd love to see you.


01:00:20.200 --> 01:00:20.800
Ah...


01:00:22.700 --> 01:00:23.500
well, um...


01:00:24.600 --> 01:00:28.100
I can't get that far away
from my mom, so...


01:00:28.200 --> 01:00:30.400
I guess we' re at an impasse.


01:00:31.000 --> 01:00:31.800
Not really.


01:00:35.200 --> 01:00:35.800
Thanks.


01:00:37.100 --> 01:00:38.400
Thanks.


01:00:38.800 --> 01:00:42.500
And the woman there said
we should have T-shirts


01:00:43.000 --> 01:00:45.500
that say
"I went hunting here"...


01:01:14.000 --> 01:01:17.000
It looks like she was having
a pretty good time stripping.


01:01:17.100 --> 01:01:20.400
Cathleen is apparently wise
beyond her years


01:01:21.600 --> 01:01:24.700
and in my expert
police chief's opinion,


01:01:25.400 --> 01:01:28.500
it hardly looks
like she was being raped.


01:01:28.800 --> 01:01:30.600
Where did you get these?


01:01:30.700 --> 01:01:32.600
I accidentally found them.


01:01:33.300 --> 01:01:34.200
Where did you find them?


01:01:34.300 --> 01:01:37.500
In a cabinet below decks
on the Lady Jane.


01:01:38.500 --> 01:01:40.700
I'd be interested
to know what you think.


01:01:40.800 --> 01:01:42.900
Do you think I should
see them, Jesse?


01:01:43.000 --> 01:01:43.600
No.


01:02:20.300 --> 01:02:22.400
Are you happy in your work?


01:02:23.500 --> 01:02:24.800
What do you mean?


01:02:25.500 --> 01:02:28.300
Well, there's this
Japanese prison camp commander


01:02:28.400 --> 01:02:29.300
in Bridge on the River Kwai


01:02:29.400 --> 01:02:33.200
and he just keeps telling these
miserable starving prisoners,


01:02:33.300 --> 01:02:35.200
"Be happy
in your work."


01:02:37.000 --> 01:02:38.900
You didn't see the movie.


01:02:39.800 --> 01:02:42.000
You happy in your work,
Cathleen?


01:02:42.100 --> 01:02:43.300
What are you talking about?


01:02:43.400 --> 01:02:48.700
The point I was attempting
to make is this is a lousy job.


01:02:50.100 --> 01:02:52.300
You need some help with that?


01:02:52.400 --> 01:02:53.000
No.


01:02:58.300 --> 01:03:01.300
Why'd you drop out
of school, Cathleen?


01:03:01.800 --> 01:03:03.100
Why are you here?


01:03:04.200 --> 01:03:05.000
You miss your mom?


01:03:05.100 --> 01:03:07.400
You've been checking up on me.


01:03:08.200 --> 01:03:08.965
I have.


01:03:09.000 --> 01:03:13.100
Don't talk to me about things
you don't know anything about.


01:03:13.200 --> 01:03:16.000
Actually,
I know something about that.


01:03:16.500 --> 01:03:17.800
Your mom run off?


01:03:18.600 --> 01:03:21.200
No, she died...
when I was eight.


01:03:23.600 --> 01:03:25.300
I miss my mom
a lot.


01:03:26.200 --> 01:03:27.600
Moms are important.


01:03:27.700 --> 01:03:31.100
Well, you don't miss
someone you never knew.


01:03:31.600 --> 01:03:34.600
You know how to do
hospital corners, Chief Stone?


01:03:34.700 --> 01:03:35.300
I do.


01:03:36.300 --> 01:03:40.600
And call me Jesse now
that you' re 18 and all grown up.


01:03:40.800 --> 01:03:42.400
What's that supposed to mean?


01:03:42.500 --> 01:03:43.600
It means
you' re not


01:03:43.700 --> 01:03:44.800
a kid anymore.


01:03:45.400 --> 01:03:47.500
It means you' re fair game.


01:03:48.200 --> 01:03:49.400
I saw the tape.


01:03:50.800 --> 01:03:51.265
So?


01:03:51.300 --> 01:03:55.400
It didn't look like anybody made
you take off your clothes.


01:03:55.500 --> 01:03:56.065
So?


01:03:56.100 --> 01:03:58.100
That's no excuse
for what he did.


01:03:58.200 --> 01:03:59.800
There's another tape.


01:04:00.700 --> 01:04:02.800
Just you
and Mr. Pendleton.


01:04:07.200 --> 01:04:10.100
He had a hidden camera
in his bedroom.


01:04:19.200 --> 01:04:21.200
I want you to tell your dad.


01:04:21.300 --> 01:04:22.300
Why should I?


01:04:24.200 --> 01:04:24.900
Because he loves you,


01:04:25.000 --> 01:04:28.000
and I don't want to see your dad
do something stupid.


01:04:28.100 --> 01:04:29.800
Unintended consequences.


01:04:30.900 --> 01:04:34.600
You' re not supposed to be here.


01:04:34.635 --> 01:04:35.265
No, I'm not.


01:04:35.300 --> 01:04:38.100
You' re not supposed to try and
talk me out of this, are you?


01:04:38.200 --> 01:04:39.300
That's correct.


01:04:40.600 --> 01:04:42.600
I could get you in trouble.


01:04:42.700 --> 01:04:43.365
You could.


01:04:43.400 --> 01:04:46.400
You don't think
what he did was wrong?


01:04:47.000 --> 01:04:49.800
It was wrong,
but it wasn't illegal.


01:04:51.500 --> 01:04:52.800
Yeah, but he's...


01:04:52.900 --> 01:04:53.700
A grownup?


01:04:55.200 --> 01:04:56.500
You know
what I think?


01:04:56.600 --> 01:04:58.400
I think you
don't like yourself


01:04:58.500 --> 01:05:00.400
so much for what you did.


01:05:00.600 --> 01:05:01.300
I think you love your dad


01:05:01.400 --> 01:05:04.000
and you know how disappointed
he'd be if he knew the truth,


01:05:04.100 --> 01:05:06.700
but you getting even
with some sick son of a bitch


01:05:06.800 --> 01:05:08.500
isn't going to change
any of that.


01:05:08.600 --> 01:05:11.400
Well, at least,
then he won't do it again.


01:05:11.500 --> 01:05:13.200
Oh, he'll do it again.


01:05:13.500 --> 01:05:14.200
Why?


01:05:14.600 --> 01:05:15.600
Because he can.


01:05:15.700 --> 01:05:18.800
And there's nothing
you or I can do to stop him.


01:05:18.900 --> 01:05:19.700
You know...


01:05:22.100 --> 01:05:24.800
you live long enough,
you have regrets.


01:05:24.900 --> 01:05:27.300
And the ones
that nag at you the most


01:05:27.400 --> 01:05:30.900
are the ones where you knew
you had a choice,


01:05:31.100 --> 01:05:34.800
the ones where you knew you
could have stopped yourself,


01:05:34.900 --> 01:05:37.000
the ones where
you looked into the mirror


01:05:37.100 --> 01:05:39.500
and everything good
inside you said,


01:05:39.600 --> 01:05:40.800
"Don't do this."


01:05:45.800 --> 01:05:49.300
You go talk to your dad and I'll
go punch him in the mouth.


01:05:49.400 --> 01:05:50.300
How's that?


01:06:20.600 --> 01:06:22.000
The Paradise Motel.


01:06:22.500 --> 01:06:23.700
I know it well.


01:06:23.900 --> 01:06:24.600
As do I.


01:06:24.900 --> 01:06:26.500
I used to live there.


01:06:26.900 --> 01:06:30.500
You' re not following me around,
are you, Terry?


01:06:30.700 --> 01:06:32.000
I prefer Terence.


01:06:32.300 --> 01:06:33.700
And I prefer you didn't do that.


01:06:33.800 --> 01:06:34.700
Do what?


01:06:35.600 --> 01:06:37.000
Follow me around, Terry.


01:06:37.100 --> 01:06:38.500
Are you trying to provoke me?


01:06:38.600 --> 01:06:41.600
I was going
to ask you the same thing.


01:06:41.700 --> 01:06:44.100
I'm just sitting here
reading the paper.


01:06:44.200 --> 01:06:47.100
Did you get that license plate
fixed, Terry?


01:06:47.200 --> 01:06:48.700
Yes, I did, Officer.


01:06:48.900 --> 01:06:51.700
And since now I have a
violation-free motor vehicle,


01:06:51.800 --> 01:06:53.700
I'll drive it wherever I want.


01:06:53.800 --> 01:06:56.000
I'll obey all traffic
regulations


01:06:56.100 --> 01:06:58.100
so as you can't harass me,


01:06:58.400 --> 01:06:59.800
unless you set me up,


01:06:59.900 --> 01:07:02.400
the way you did my brother
when you killed him.


01:07:02.500 --> 01:07:05.100
I didn't kill your brother,
Terry,


01:07:05.600 --> 01:07:08.200
but I did set him up
pretty good.


01:07:17.300 --> 01:07:18.500
God, I miss her.


01:07:23.300 --> 01:07:24.000
Scotch?


01:07:24.200 --> 01:07:25.200
For the lady.


01:07:25.800 --> 01:07:26.600
Thank you.


01:07:28.500 --> 01:07:29.300
Thank you.


01:07:30.800 --> 01:07:31.900
Long way back?


01:07:35.500 --> 01:07:36.300
It is.


01:07:36.800 --> 01:07:38.100
Thanks for meeting me halfway.


01:07:38.200 --> 01:07:41.800
Well, actually, it's three
quarters to one quarter,


01:07:41.900 --> 01:07:43.600
so I guess you owe me.


01:07:45.700 --> 01:07:49.600
Are you going to find the man
who killed my sister?


01:07:51.500 --> 01:07:52.900
Well, it's been 15 years.


01:07:53.000 --> 01:07:54.700
How long have
you been on it?


01:07:54.800 --> 01:07:55.600
Three days.


01:07:55.800 --> 01:07:58.700
That's not actually
why I called you.


01:07:58.900 --> 01:08:00.300
Why'd you call me?


01:08:00.900 --> 01:08:04.000
The soup of the day
is cream of tomato.


01:08:04.600 --> 01:08:05.400
Thank you.


01:08:10.100 --> 01:08:12.100
You know, I wasn't
being entirely honest


01:08:12.200 --> 01:08:13.500
